From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qwqgong-ui <noreply@qwqgong-ui.local>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 10:36:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] h2mux: give the CONNECT request a header map

The request the client session builds for each stream is a bare
http.Request literal with no Header, and RoundTrip rejects that with
"http: nil Request.Header" as soon as x/net/http2 routes through
net/http's request validation, which it does from x/net v0.54.0 when
built with a Go 1.27 toolchain. Every h2mux stream then fails to open:
the caller sees a closed pipe on the request body and a timeout waiting
for response headers.

A nil Header was never valid on an http.Request; the older x/net/http2
implementation just happened not to look. Give it an empty map.
---
 h2mux.go | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/h2mux.go b/h2mux.go
index 97520f9..b6a872a 100644
--- a/h2mux.go
+++ b/h2mux.go
@@ -203,6 +203,7 @@ func (s *h2MuxClientSession) Open(tcpTimeout time.Duration) (net.Conn, error) {
 		Method: http.MethodConnect,
 		Body:   pipeInReader,
 		URL:    &url.URL{Scheme: "https", Host: "localhost"},
+		Header: make(http.Header),
 	}
 	connCtx, cancel := context.WithCancel(context.Background())
 	request = request.WithContext(connCtx)
